  "findings": [
    "Contract type is the strongest business lever: month-to-month customers churn at 45.9% versus 3.5% on two-year contracts.",
    "Churn is concentrated among new customers: 51.4% churn in the first 12 months versus 4.4% after 4 years.",
    "The model relies mainly on Contract, tenure, InternetService; fibre-optic (42.2%) and electronic-check payers (32.6%) show above-average churn (overall 28.2%)."
  ],
  "business_recommendation": "Route customers scored HIGH risk (probability >= 0.65) to a retention team; offer discounted 1-2 year contracts to month-to-month customers, build a first-12-months onboarding programme, investigate fibre-optic service quality, and encourage automatic payment methods and security/support add-ons.",
  "limitations": [
    "The dataset used here is a schema-identical replica of the IBM Telco data - re-run with the official CSV to obtain official metrics.",
    "Single historical snapshot: no time dimension, so seasonality and trends are not captured.",
    "The model shows association, not causation - a discount is not guaranteed to change behaviour.",
    "Probabilities from a class-weighted model are not calibrated; use them for ranking, not as exact percentages.",
    "Retention cost / customer lifetime value were not in the data, so the ideal risk threshold is a business assumption.",
    "A prediction is not certainty: a share of flagged customers would not have left."
  ],
